# Converter

- Keep filesystem, archive, network, and database I/O outside converter-core.
- Use explicit decode, normalize, validate, map, canonicalize, and emit stages.
- Return typed IR plus diagnostics; do not throw for expected malformed input.
- Version IR and validate it at production and consumption boundaries.
- Derive import IDs from canonical semantic identity and algorithm version only.
- Never read current time, randomness, locale, environment, or process globals.
- Canonically sort output where source order is not semantic.
- Preserve unknown safe fields only in bounded, namespaced extensions.
- Reject unsupported source/version combinations explicitly.
- Golden-test output, diagnostics, deterministic IDs, and repeated-run equivalence.
